					'tab_content' => '<p>HTML5 apps provide a convenient way of developing mobile applications that can run on multiple platforms. These apps are a set of web pages that are specifically designed for mobile devices. They come with a plethora of advanced features, such as streaming video and audio data, handling graphics and animation, and offline support. Additionally, they offer semantic elements, form controls, multimedia components, and various APIs that support geolocation services, drag-and-drop operations, local application caching, and much more.<br /><br />HTML5 rarely works independently. Most HTML5 applications incorporate Cascading Style Sheets (CSS), which determine how the HTML elements are displayed on a browser, and JavaScript, which includes the APIs for handling text, objects, and arrays. These technologies are supported by all major browsers, making it possible to develop web-based applications that can run on a wide range of devices.</p>',
